                                "sense_id": "6356334b-6e77-3a11-adb4-25a7a6f127bd",
                                "text": "Hail, many-colour’d messenger, that ne'er\nDost disobey the wife of Jupiter;\nWho with thy saffron wings upon my flowers\nDiffusest honey-drops, refreshing showers,\nAnd with each end of thy blue bow dost crown\nMy bosky acres and my unshrubb’d down,\nRich scarf to my proud earth;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "02f634b5-e6ad-47c2-8394-497d293afa2c",
                                "sense_id": "6356334b-6e77-3a11-adb4-25a7a6f127bd",
                                "text": "From the spot he’s left her in, a blank, unshrubbed bit of service-yard where the earth is worn bald, she can see printed in black cut-out and lamp-glow, her own house."
                            }
                        ]
